cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this exercise, please cite it as below. The model it runs has its own citation; see the primacy-premium repository."
title: "Committee Exercise: a four-seat budget exercise on the estimated model of The Primacy Premium, 2026 to 2035"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Agard
    given-names: Alyssa I.
version: 2.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alyssaagard/primacy-committee-exercise"
url: "https://primacy.alyssaagard.dev/committee-exercise/"
abstract: >-
  A browser exercise in which up to four committees set real military
  expenditure for the United States, China, NATO Europe, and the
  Indo-Pacific allies over five periods to 2035. Commitments are sealed and
  simultaneous, the record publishes with its real lags, and interval
  statements are scored. Seats without a committee, the remaining blocks,
  and the reserve currency shares are run by the estimated model of The
  Primacy Premium, release 1.1.0. The engine is checked against the
  published medians of that release.
keywords:
  - conditional forecasting
  - wargaming
  - defense economics
  - defense policy
  - military expenditure
  - burden sharing
  - reserve currencies
  - interval scoring
references:
